      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nEvery user who lets their lock reach its natural expiry loses 100% of their rewards for the final epoch in which they were bonded. The reward system snapshots `userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd` at the exact `epochTimestampEnd` timestamp.\n\nAs `veTRUST` balance decays linearly to zero at lock expiry, and the lock-end is always <= the epoch-end (due to week-rounding), the snapshot returns *zero* for the *epoch in which the lock expires*. The user was bonded for a part or all of that epoch, yet received nothing.\n\nThis affects **100% of locks that reach their natural expiry** without manual extension to unlock time.\n\nFor the worst case, users who lock for any duration `<= epochLength` (including the minimum allowed e.g `MINTIME = epochLength = 14 days`) can lose **100% of their rewards**, since the lock can start and expire within the same epoch, leaving no epoch where the end-snapshot captures a non-zero balance.\n\n### Detailed description\n\nThe claim system rule from [TrustBonding.sol - Natspec](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/src/protocol/emissions/TrustBonding.sol#L28-L29)\n> _\"Rewards for epoch `n` become claimable in epoch `n+1` and are forfeited if not claimed before the next epoch ends\n> (i.e. only the previous epoch's rewards are claimable).\"_\n\n`claimRewards` always computes for `prevEpoch = currentEpoch - 1` and evaluates the user's balance at\n`epochTimestampEnd(prevEpoch)`:\n\n```solidity\n// TrustBonding.sol\nuint256 prevEpoch = currentEpochLocal - 1;\nuint256 rawUserRewards = _userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(msg.sender, prevEpoch);\n```\nwhich calls \n\n```solidity\n// TrustBonding.sol\nuint256 userBalance = userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(account, epoch);\nuint256 totalBalance = totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(epoch);\nif (userBalance == 0 || totalBalance == 0) {\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn userBalance * _emissionsForEpoch(epoch) / totalBalance;\n```\n\nAnd `userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd` snapshots at the exact epoch-end timestamp:\n\n```solidity\n// TrustBonding.sol\nreturn _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch));\n```\n\nWhere `_balanceOf` computes linearly decaying voting power that reaches exactly zero at lock expiry:\n\n```solidity\n// VotingEscrow.sol L636-643\nfunction _balanceOf(address addr, uint256 _t) internal view returns (uint256) {\n    uint256 target_epoch = _find_user_timestamp_epoch(addr, _t, user_point_epoch[addr]);\n    Point memory point = user_point_history[addr][target_epoch];\n    point.bias -= point.slope * int128(int256(_t) - int256(point.ts));\n    if (point.bias < 0) {\n        point.bias = 0;\n    }\n    return uint256(int256(point.bias));\n}\n```\n\nThis will affect every epoch in which the lock expires.\n\nFor example: Consider a user whose lock expires during epoch N \n```\n     Epoch N-1              Epoch N (lock expires here)       Epoch N+1\n|───────────────|─────────────────────|──────────────────|\n    user is bonded          user is bonded, balance          lock expired,\n                            decays to 0 at lock_end          balance = 0\n```\n- **Epoch N-1 rewards**: Captured at `epochTimestampEnd(N-1)`. Lock hasn't expired, balance > 0. Rewards claimable during epoch N. This works fine.\n- **Epoch N rewards**: The user was bonded for part or all of epoch N. But the snapshot is at `epochTimestampEnd(N)`, by which point `locked.end <= epochTimestampEnd(N)`, so `_balanceOf` returns **0**. `_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch` returns 0. The user **can never claim** epoch N rewards — they are gone.\n\n### Impact\n\n1. Guaranteed loss of the final epoch's rewards for every expiring lock. This is not probabilistic, any\nlock that reaches its `locked.end` loses 100% of rewards for the epoch in which it expires.\n2. Up to 100% total reward loss for lockers with duration <= epochLength\n3. Contradicts documented design - The NatSpec promises rewards \"allocated pro rata to users' shares of the total bonded balance.\" A user bonded for an entire epoch receiving 0% of their share violates this guarantee.\n4. No mitigation without cost - the only escape is extending the lock (more capital lockup than intended), and the user has no way to know they need to do this.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nInstead of snapshotting balance at the exact `epochTimestampEnd` (where the linear decay has already zeroed out), the reward calculation should detect when a user's lock expires within the epoch and sample their balance at `locked.end - 1`(the last second they were bonded). \n\nThis captures the user's non-zero balance at the moment just before expiry and gives them proportional credit for the time they were bonded during that epoch.\n\nModify `_userEligibleRewardsForEpoch` to compare the user's `locked.end` against the epoch boundary:\n\n```solidity\nfunction _userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(address account, uint256 epoch) internal view returns (uint256) {\n    if (account == address(0)) {\n        revert TrustBonding_ZeroAddress();\n    }\n    if (epoch > currentEpoch()) {\n        revert TrustBonding_InvalidEpoch();\n    }\n\n    uint256 epochEnd = _epochTimestampEnd(epoch);\n    uint256 epochStart = epochEnd - ICoreEmissionsController(satelliteEmissionsController).getEpochLength();\n    uint256 lockEnd = locked[account].end;\n\n    uint256 snapshotTime = epochEnd;\n    // If the user's lock expires within this epoch, snapshot just before expiry\n    // instead of at epochEnd where balance has already decayed to zero.\n    if (lockEnd > epochStart && lockEnd <= epochEnd) {\n        snapshotTime = lockEnd - 1;\n    }\n\n    uint256 userBalance = _balanceOf(account, snapshotTime);\n    uint256 totalBalance = _totalSupply(epochEnd);\n\n    if (userBalance == 0 || totalBalance == 0) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    return userBalance * _emissionsForEpoch(epoch) / totalBalance;\n}\n```\nThis ensures users who were bonded during the epoch receive their fair share of rewards proportional to their bonded balance, rather than getting zero due to the snapshot timing coinciding with exact lock expiry.",
      "proofOfConcept": "/// User bonded for an entire epoch gets ZERO rewards because\n/// their lock expiry (WEEK-rounded) falls at or before the epoch-end\n/// snapshot, and hence their claim reverts.\n\n//@dev place the following test case in [ClaimRewards.t.sol](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/314b7d4d9ccbaf27e4484a6c0706af83d3f75f36/tests/unit/TrustBonding/ClaimRewards.t.sol#L499)\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_poc_zeroRewards_lockExpiresAtEpochEnd() external {\n        uint256 epoch0End = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(0);\n        uint256 epochLength = protocol.trustBonding.epochLength();\n        uint256 epoch1End = epoch0End + epochLength;\n\n        uint256 lockAmount = 1000 ether;\n\n        // Alice: lock expires at WEEK-rounded epoch1End (always <= epoch1End)\n        _createLockWithDuration(users.alice, lockAmount, epoch1End);\n        (, uint256 aliceLockEnd) = protocol.trustBonding.locked(users.alice);\n        assertLe(aliceLockEnd, epoch1End, \"Lock end <= epoch end after WEEK rounding\");\n\n        // Bob: same amount, 2-year lock (control)\n        _createLock(users.bob, lockAmount);\n\n        // Alice has real bonded balance DURING the epoch\n        vm.warp(epoch0End + epochLength / 2);\n        uint256 aliceMidBalance = protocol.trustBonding.balanceOfAtT(users.alice, block.timestamp);\n        assertGt(aliceMidBalance, 0, \"Alice is bonded mid-epoch\");\n\n        // Advance to epoch 2 (epoch 1 rewards now claimable)\n        _advanceToEpoch(2);\n\n        // At the epoch-end snapshot, Alice's balance has decayed to 0\n        uint256 aliceEndBalance = protocol.trustBonding.userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(users.alice, 1);\n        assertEq(aliceEndBalance, 0, \"Alice epoch-end balance is zero\");\n\n        // Alice gets 0 rewards, Bob gets 100%\n        uint256 aliceRewards = protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.alice, 1);\n        uint256 bobRewards = protocol.trustBonding.userEligibleRewardsForEpoch(users.bob, 1);\n        assertEq(aliceRewards, 0, \"Alice gets ZERO rewards despite full-epoch bonding\");\n        assertGt(bobRewards, 0, \"Bob absorbs Alice's share\");\n\n        // Alice's claim reverts\n        resetPrank(users.alice);\n        vm.expectRevert(abi.encodeWithSelector(ITrustBonding.TrustBonding_NoRewardsToClaim.selector));\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.alice);\n    }\n\n```",
